@@ -1,2 +1,13 @@
 # textkit
 Zero-dependency string helpers (ESM). Tests: `npm test` (Node built-in runner).
+
+- `slugify(input)` — lowercase, ASCII-alphanumeric, hyphen-separated slug.
+- `wrap(text, width = 80)` — wrap on whitespace (runs of spaces, tabs and newlines collapse to one
+  space); words longer than `width` are hard-broken so no line exceeds `width`. `width` must be an
+  integer ≥ 1 (else `RangeError`).
+- `truncate(text, max, ellipsis = "…")` — at most `max` characters including the ellipsis; text that
+  already fits is returned unchanged. If the ellipsis alone is longer than `max`, it is itself cut to
+  `max`. `max` must be an integer ≥ 0 (else `RangeError`).
+
+"Characters" means Unicode code points: surrogate pairs (e.g. emoji) are never split. Multi-code-point
+grapheme clusters (ZWJ emoji sequences, combining marks) may be split.
